OVERVIEW: Search for DICOM objects using QIDO-RS

Searches for studies, series, or instances on DICOMweb server.

Examples:
  dicom-wado query https://server/dicom-web --patient-name "DOE*"
  dicom-wado query https://server/dicom-web --study-date 20240101-20240131
  dicom-wado query https://server/dicom-web --modality CT --limit 10
  dicom-wado query https://server/dicom-web --level series --study 1.2.3.4.5

USAGE: dicom-wado query [<options>] <base-url>

ARGUMENTS:
  <base-url>              DICOMweb server base URL

OPTIONS:
  --level <level>         Query level: study, series, instance (default: study)
                          (default: study)
  --patient-name <patient-name>
                          Patient name (wildcards * and ? supported)
  --patient-id <patient-id>
                          Patient ID
  --study-date <study-date>
                          Study date or range (YYYYMMDD or YYYYMMDD-YYYYMMDD)
  --study <study>         Study Instance UID: a single UID scopes
                          series/instance paths; a comma-separated list remains
                          a matching filter
  --series <series>       Series Instance UID: a single UID with --study scopes
                          instance paths; a comma-separated list remains a
                          matching filter
  --accession-number <accession-number>
                          Accession number
  --modality <modality>   Modality filter (0008,0060) — e.g. CT, MR, US, OPT.
                          Run 'dicom-tags --list-modalities' for every DICOM
                          2026a code.
  --strict-modality       Reject a --modality value that is not a current DICOM
                          Defined Term
  --study-description <study-description>
                          Study description
  --pps-start-date <pps-start-date>
                          Series attribute (series or relational instance
                          searches): Performed Procedure Step Start Date
                          (0040,0244), YYYYMMDD or a YYYYMMDD-YYYYMMDD range
  --pps-start-time <pps-start-time>
                          Series attribute (series or relational instance
                          searches): Performed Procedure Step Start Time
                          (0040,0245), HHMMSS or an HHMMSS-HHMMSS range
  --sps-id <sps-id>       Series attribute (series or relational instance
                          searches): Scheduled Procedure Step ID inside Request
                          Attributes Sequence (0040,0275.0040,0009)
  --requested-procedure-id <requested-procedure-id>
                          Series attribute (series or relational instance
                          searches): Requested Procedure ID inside Request
                          Attributes Sequence (0040,0275.0040,1001)
  --limit <limit>         Maximum number of results (default: 100) (default:
                          100)
  --offset <offset>       Offset for pagination (default: 0) (default: 0)
  --fuzzy-matching        Ask for fuzzy matching of person names (PS3.18
                          8.3.4.2: fuzzymatching=true)
  --token <token>         OAuth2 bearer token for authentication
  -f, --format <format>   Output format: table, json, csv, dicom-json (default:
                          table). dicom-json is the PS3.18 F.2 DICOM JSON
                          Model; json is a tool summary (keyword keys)
                          (default: table)
  --verbose               Show verbose output
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

